cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "invasimapr: Workflow to Visualise Trait Dispersion and Assess Invasibility"
version: 0.2.0
type: software
abstract: >-
  invasimapr is an R package for quantifying and mapping community-level
  invasion fitness and site-specific invasibility. It links species
  occurrences, functional traits and environmental data to build a shared
  trait-environment space, fit resident community models, and decompose
  invasion fitness into abiotic suitability, niche crowding and resident
  competition. The package returns species invasiveness, site invasibility
  and trait-effect indicators, together with maps and plots that support
  evidence-based biodiversity management and policy planning.
